<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">County Galway</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">County <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galway">Galway</a> is a county in the province of Connacht in the west of Ireland, with the city of Galway as its centre. It includes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connemara">Connemara</a>, the Aran Islands and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lough-corrib">Lough Corrib</a>. Its eastern part was the core of the Gaelic kingdom of Uí Maine, ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/o-ceallaigh">O'Kellys</a>, while the city was founded by the Anglo-Norman de Burghs.</p></div>
